/**
\fn ISerializer& pdg::ISerializer::setResourceMode(int mode)
\brief Choose whether saved image resources are embedded or externally referenced.
\param mode `serialization_Complete` (the default) embeds pixels;
`serialization_ExternalReferences` permits named file/resource references.
\return This writer. An invalid constant throws without changing the policy.

The policy belongs to this writer and does not change other writers. Set it before
writing data. Serializer rejects a policy change after its first write. Each image
record identifies its representation, so readers need no matching setting.
Anonymous runtime images and images changed through setTransparentColor() or mutable
getData() access are embedded in either mode. ImageStrip frame layout, opacity,
edge clamping and subsection/frame views are preserved. Shared source images remain
shared when written with serialize_obj(). Initial Sprite frame records use the same policy for artwork and collision masks.
Resource policy does not change the
serialization flags that select which object state to save.

External identifiers use the original `file:` path or `res:` resource name. The
reader resolves them through the filesystem or ResourceManager; missing sources
and changed dimensions throw an error identifying the resource. Complete records
load independently of their original files and resource cache.

\note Runtime-created and modified images retain their pixels. Named images may
reload pixels while saving a complete record; call Image::retainData() before
drawing if the original resource will become unavailable before the save. A
complete save fails explicitly if pixels cannot be recovered. It never substitutes
an external reference. Discard a writer after a failed serialization operation.

\code{.cpp}
Serializer writer;
writer.setResourceMode(serialization_Complete);
writer.serialize_obj(image);  // an existing Image*; bytes belong to writer
// For a smaller save that resolves named assets on load, select
// serialization_ExternalReferences before writing to a new Serializer.
\endcode
\sa ISerializer::getResourceMode(), Image::serialize()
*/

/**
\fn int pdg::ISerializer::getResourceMode() const
\brief Return this writer's resource policy.
\return `serialization_Complete` or `serialization_ExternalReferences`.
*/

/**
\fn uint32 pdg::Image::getSerializedSize(ISerializer* serializer) const
\brief Measure an image record under the writer's resource policy.
\param serializer Writer that will receive the record; must not be null.
\return Record size in bytes, excluding the stream header and enclosing object's tag/length.
Sizing validates availability of embedded pixels and may reload a named image.
Embedded records support RGB/RGBA pixels, dimensions up to 32768 on each axis,
and at most 512 MiB of pixel data.
\sa Image::serialize(), ISerializer::setResourceMode()
*/

/**
\fn void pdg::Image::serialize(ISerializer* serializer) const
\brief Write image pixels or a resolvable resource reference with image settings.
\param serializer Destination writer; must not be null.
The writer's resource mode selects the representation. Anonymous and modified
images embed their pixels even when references are allowed. Frame/subsection
images retain references to their source image within the saved graph.
\note This writes a raw image record. Read it with Image::deserialize(). Use
ISerializer::serialize_obj() and IDeserializer::deserialize_obj() when the stream
should also construct the image and preserve object identity automatically.
\sa ISerializer::setResourceMode(), Image::getSerializedSize()
*/

/**
\fn void pdg::Image::deserialize(IDeserializer* deserializer)
\brief Replace this image from an embedded or external-resource image record.
\param deserializer Reader positioned at a raw image record; must not be null.
The record supplies its own resource policy. Loading preserves strip frame layout,
opacity, edge clamping and subsection selection; decoded pixels remain available.
Malformed records, unavailable resources and changed resource dimensions throw.
Validation completes before replacing this image's existing content. Referenced
parent images are retained until this image is destroyed or replaced.
\sa Image::serialize(), ISerializer::setResourceMode()
*/
